These are '''review priorities''', not a claim that every other article already satisfies K01. The full 302-object snapshot needs an independent article-by-article purpose review. Prior title/keyword screening is useful for selecting questions but is not a substitute for inspecting mechanisms, uses, references and context.

== Review record ==

For each page, record the editorial outcome, computational mechanism or method, relevant observing/measuring evidence, whether independent identity is needed, and whether linked Simple/Technical variants and semantic edges require reconciliation. Update the record as each page is actually reviewed. No review outcome is assigned to these candidates by creating this register.

== Release boundary ==

GitHub <code>main</code> is the integrated source; staging compilation and CI cannot approve K01, publish changes to the live MediaWiki or remove existing site pages. Re-scope should proceed through bounded, reviewed changes with explicit dependency and redirect considerations when renaming or contextualizing a canonical page.

